~ start
Brian: Dan? Dan!!
Dan: Brian? Thank god. What's going on. Where did you all disappear
Brian: Don't know, last thing I remember is us four entering the house, and than all being alone and all this madness
Dan: We need to find a way out, and fast. I feel like my mind is going crazy just from being here
Brian: Agreed. Whitch way?
Dan: No idea. I have been walking this hallway for ages. Seems endles. The doors are all lock.
Dan: And they seem to shif colours too
Brian: Any strategy on getting out
Dan: Well, you managed to enter, so some doors must be unlocked. Just have to find out whitch
do SignalManager.fear.emit(1)
=> END

~ start1
Brian: Seems that just randomly trying doors will not get us anywhere
Dan: Maybe, but what else can we do
Brian: Let's think about it. What colour was the door you entered throught
Dan: Red! No, wait.. yellow? brown? green? Can't recall... 
Dan: Must be this place getting to me
Brian: I entered through brown
Brian: and from what I've seen, the doors in the house are also brown
Brian: lets try the brown doors and see if those work
do SignalManager.fear.emit(2)

=> END

~ start2
Dan: No luck either
Brian: Yea
Dan: Maybe, we are looking at it wrong
Dan: the doors change, if you walk back and forth, their colour is not what it was
Dan: Maybe, the real door does not change colour
Dan: Maybe we should keep an eye out, ad see whitch stays the same
do SignalManager.fear.emit(2)

=> END

~ start3
Brian: Well, still no way out
Dan: I am starting to think, we won't make it
Brian: No, no don't say that
Brian: Think. Brown doors lead out. But doors here change colour...
Dan: What if, we combine our theories?
Brian: You mean, a brown door that stays brown?
Dan: Yea, I mean, those are quite rare, it's worth a shot
Brian: True. And since some doors in this place are locked after entery, maybe we should try a few more
Brian: If we give up after one, we might just find the locked one and miss the opened one
do SignalManager.fear.emit(3)

=> END

~ start4
Dan: I think we should stop trying
Brian: Yea, I know. I just don't want to give up yet
Dan: Maybe there is something we are not seeing
Dan: But I think it is more likely we are trapped
Brian: I am sorry...
Dan: For what?
Brian: I was the one who suggested exploring this house
Brian: And now all of you are in this maddness
Brian: Thanks to me
Dan: Don't be
Brian: Why not?
Dan: You had no idea what would happen
Dan: And you are just as trapped as we are
Dan: From where I am standing, we either both escape
Dan: And that you have nothing to appologise to me for
Dan: Or we both loose ourselves here
Dan: And than I'd say we are equal
Dan: You chose to explore this house
Dan: We chose to explore it with you
Dan: We both pay the price
Dan: Not like it's any fair
Dan: But thats life
Brian: But if we get out, Margaret and Alice still migh not..
Dan: You missunderstand me
Dan: You do not escape blame by getting killed with us
Dan: You do not deserve it either way
Dan: You are a good person Brian
Dan: You are not responcible for the horrors of this place. I am sure of that
Brian: (maybe he is right)
Brian: (I do share their fate)
Brian: (I couldn't have know what this place was)
Brian: (And it seems to torment me just like them)
Brian: Thank you.
Brian: You are right, we make it out together, or die together
Brian: But I won't leave you
Brian: Now, what do we do about the door situations
Dan: I think we exhausted all the door options
Dan: Only think left is to walk the hall
Dan: Perhaps it is not infinite, just really long
Dan: Or perhaps we will find something to aid us
Brian: Ok, we walk
Brian: Just stay close, don't get lost, ok?
Dan: Right behind you.
do SignalManager.fear.emit(-5)

=> END

~ cycle
Dan: Need a break?
- yes
	Dan: Ok, we can rest for a while
	Dan: Not like there is any immediate danger
	Dan: And we have been walking for quite some time
	Brian: (How long have we been waking for)
	Brian: (minutes?, hours?, day?)
	Brian: (best not dwell on that)
- no
	Dan: Than lets keep walking
do SignalManager.fear.emit(6)

=> END
